### Area 4: the role-permission matrix, masking and the rules for data sent to AI.
### Sign in first (requests/auth.http), then paste the op_csrf cookie value below.
### Reading the matrix needs roles.read; changing it needs roles.manage (SYSTEM_ADMIN
### holds both, AUDITOR holds roles.read). Any other role gets 403 FORBIDDEN with a
### traceId, and the refusal is audited.
@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000
@csrf = paste the op_csrf cookie value here after signing in

### Every role with its permissions and data scope, the permissions in display order,
### and the cells that cannot change (the system admin never approves, posts or pays).
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/governance/matrix

### Grant or revoke one permission. Audited. Granting twice changes and audits nothing.
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/governance/matrix/FINANCE/permissions/orders.read
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{ "granted": true }

### A locked cell: the system admin cannot be given payments.post. Answers 409.
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/governance/matrix/SYSTEM_ADMIN/permissions/payments.post
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{ "granted": true }

### Which records a role may see: all, brands or own. Stored only: no list reads it
### yet, so the matrix screen does not offer it (#268, ADR 0065).
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/governance/matrix/PRODUCT_MANAGER/data-scope
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{ "dataScope": "brands" }

### Make one role hold exactly the permissions another holds. Its data scope stays as it was.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/governance/matrix/copy
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{ "fromRole": "FINANCE", "toRole": "LOGISTICS" }

### Synthetic customers with the sample masking rule applied for YOUR role.
### Sign in as WAREHOUSE and the note comes back as null, with the reason.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/governance/masking/sample

### What data may go to which AI provider. The default is synthetic data only.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/governance/ai-destinations

### Ask about one request, as the AI gateway will. Real data is refused with a reason.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/governance/ai-destinations/check
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{ "provider": "bedrock", "classification": "internal", "origin": "real" }

### F-5: bank-detail holds. No route here takes or returns a full bank number.
### Put a hold's id in holdId. Reading needs workflows.read, and masks by role.
@holdId = 00000000-0000-7000-8000-000000000000

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/governance/bank-holds?status=open&page=1&pageSize=25

### One hold: which fields differ, the last four by role, and why it cannot move.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/governance/bank-holds/{{holdId}}

### As FINANCE, not the person who changed the details. Who verified comes from
### the session. A confirmation needs a contact taken from the stored record.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/governance/bank-holds/{{holdId}}/verifications
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{ "outcome": "confirmed", "contactedAt": "2026-11-10T09:00:00.000Z", "contactFromStoredRecord": true, "reason": "Called the number on the stored vendor record." }

### A rejected verification keeps the hold, and records why.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/governance/bank-holds/{{holdId}}/verifications
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{ "outcome": "rejected", "contactedAt": "2026-11-10T09:00:00.000Z", "contactFromStoredRecord": true, "reason": "The vendor says it did not change its account." }

### As a management approver, not the verifier and not the person who changed the details.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/governance/bank-holds/{{holdId}}/clear
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{ "resolution": "accept-new-details", "reason": "The verification is sound and the change is genuine." }

### After a rejected verification: the stored details stand, recorded as suspected fraud.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/governance/bank-holds/{{holdId}}/clear
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{ "resolution": "keep-stored-details", "reason": "The vendor denies the change, so the PI is not genuine." }
